::journey-timeline

### Teenage Tinkering
It started with MySpace profile customization and shamelessly view-sourcing every site I loved. Building my first "Hello World" page felt like magic—creating something from nothing but text in a file.

### Formal Education & First Roles
Computer science gave me the theory: algorithms, data structures, systems. The real learning happened in internships and first roles where communication, product thinking, and collaboration mattered as much as clean code.

### Product Engineering & Tattoo Discovery
Years of product engineering across healthcare, fintech, and e-commerce taught me how to ship reliable software. Around that time I fell in love with tattooing—a creative counterpart that sharpened my sense of detail, balance, and storytelling.

### Present Day
I balance software engineering with tattoo artistry, open-source hardware projects, and writing. Violet and our chinchillas keep me grounded, and I stay energized by the communities around custom keyboards, Nuxt, and creative tooling.

